      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFix the sequence-parallel layout in the non-mHC branch of `Glm5NextDecoderLayer.forward()`.\n\n`Glm5NextModel` shards tokens before entering decoder layers. The non-mHC branch passes that shard directly to attention without gathering the full sequence or reduce-scattering its output. MoE then shards the input a second time. This produces incorrect dense-layer outputs and can cause a token-count mismatch in expert dispatch.\n\nFollow the existing mHC layout: gather and trim padding before attention, reduce-scatter afterward, and tell MoE that its input is already sequence-parallel. MTP receives full-sequence inputs, so it skips these outer collectives and retains MoE's internal chunk/gather pair. The mHC branch is unchanged.\n\nSearches for GLM sequence-parallel fixes found no open PR addressing this non-mHC decoder layout.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nRun a four-process numerical regression with TP=2, DP=2 and expert parallelism, alongside the existing sequence-parallel tests. Compare sequence-sharded execution against a replicated-token reference using randomly initialized GLM decoder layers, the real dense/MoE implementations, weight post-processing and NCCL collectives. Attention uses a small causal SDPA fixture with the real TP output projection.\n\nCover dense and sparse layers, 1/5/8 tokens, padding, and MTP's full-sequence inputs. BF16 comparisons use `rtol=atol=0.02`.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/models/glm5next/test_sequence_parallel.py -v --tb=short\n```\n\nCheck the changed production file:\n\n```bash\npre-commit run --hook-stage manual --files vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\nFour A100 80GB GPUs, Python 3.10.12, PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130, NCCL 2.32.3, `CompilationMode.NONE`; numerical comparisons against `e440b75`:\n\n| Version | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Original | 1 failed, 3 passed; dense-layer numerical mismatch with one token |\n| MoE flag only | 1 failed, 3 passed; dense-layer mismatch remains |\n| Attention collectives only | 1 failed, 3 passed; token-count assertion in MoE dispatch |\n| Complete fix | 4 passed |\n\nPre-commit checks pass for the changed production file, including Ruff and mypy for Python 3.10–3.13.\n\nThe fix was developed with assistance from GPT-6. The changes have been reviewed by a human.\n",
